  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nAs with previous discussion, the outlook remains favorable for\nsurface high pressure and varying degrees of upper riding into \nearly next week; expect near to above normal high temperature \nwith potential for larger diurnal swings, dry weather, a \npreponderance of sunshine and periodic occurrences of morning \nfrost (favoring where the growing season has ended). This is \nbest highlighted by the LREF (an ensemble model) which shows the\nprobability for measurable rainfall AT ANY TIME between now and\n2pm Monday being less than 15%.\n\nThe previous discourse about non-zero rain chances with an upper\nshortwave passage late Wednesday night into Thursday is grasping\nfor air given little change to the anomalously dry atmosphere\n(PWATs remain near the 10th percentile), meaning enough model\nprecip feedback is likely to be a (brief) increase in mid level\nclouds.",
